### Reproduction steps

1. Use Linux system with Podman. In my case I use RHEL 10, I don't know how OS specific this could be.
2. Clone https://github.com/bkhl/zed-devcontainer-issue.git
3. Open Zed and open the project. When asked, tell it to open dev container. Alternately use the `projects: open dev container` command from the command palette.

### Current vs. Expected behavior

Current: A modal pops up with the text: "Failed to start Dev Container. See logs for details. DevContainer creation failed"

<img width="407" height="252" alt="Screenshot of modal" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ec40d3e2-95b7-4937-9775-75092036928a" />

In the Zed log I see these errors:

```
2026-05-18T16:05:28+07:00 ERROR [dev_container::docker] Non-success result from docker pull: Trying to pull localhost/zediss-c1fb072bcf3a6e9e-features:latest...
time="2026-05-18T16:05:25+07:00" level=warning msg="Failed, retrying in 1s ... (1/3). Error: initializing source docker://localhost/zediss-c1fb072bcf3a6e9e-features:latest: pinging container registry localhost: Get \"https://localhost/v2/\": dial tcp [::1]:443: connect: connection refused"
time="2026-05-18T16:05:26+07:00" level=warning msg="Failed, retrying in 1s ... (2/3). Error: initializing source docker://localhost/zediss-c1fb072bcf3a6e9e-features:latest: pinging container registry localhost: Get \"https://localhost/v2/\": dial tcp [::1]:443: connect: connection refused"
time="2026-05-18T16:05:27+07:00" level=warning msg="Failed, retrying in 1s ... (3/3). Error: initializing source docker://localhost/zediss-c1fb072bcf3a6e9e-features:latest: pinging container registry localhost: Get \"https://localhost/v2/\": dial tcp [::1]:443: connect: connection refused"
Error: unable to copy from source docker://localhost/zediss-c1fb072bcf3a6e9e-features:latest: initializing source docker://localhost/zediss-c1fb072bcf3a6e9e-features:latest: pinging container registry localhost: Get "https://localhost/v2/": dial tcp [::1]:443: connect: connection refused
```

(See full `Zed.log` below)

Expected: Devcontainer starts and project is reopened in the container.

Note: the most recent version where this container works for me is Zed `0.233.10`, but using that is a non-starter for me as in that version there are other bugs that affects me. I thought the issue was similar to https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/54925 so was waiting for that to be resolved, but it now seems this is something different.

